3. Model weights
----------------
This repository contains no model weights. The reference pipeline was validated with:

  * Anima DiT (image generation backbone), and the MiaoMiao Harem anime fine-tune
    distributed through Civitai.
  * Wan2.1 VAE decoder, as shipped in the ComfyUI ecosystem (`qwen_image_vae`).
  * Qwen3-0.6B, and the T5 tokenizer used by ComfyUI's text encoders.

Each of these is governed by its own upstream license and acceptable-use terms.
Nothing here grants you rights to them, and the numbers in this repository's docs
say nothing about whether your use of those weights is permitted.


4. Reference work: mtk-npug-handoff
-----------------------------------
An independent community project (https://github.com/bestkojima/mtk-npug-handoff)
explores a different format ("NPUG") for the same hardware family. It was read as
reference material. No code from it is included here, and it is not redistributed.

The two projects are unrelated: KAtorch uses its own plain-text graph format and
drives the Neuron adapter API directly.


5. Deliberately not distributed
-------------------------------
  * Vendor shared objects, sysroots, and headers (proprietary; see section 1).
  * Any `.dla` compiled network, APK, keystore, or model checkpoint.
  * The PC-side debug environment that runs the vendor's closed-source compiler under
    emulation and patches it at runtime. That environment is a local reverse-engineering
    aid; it exists to keep this repository free of vendor binaries.
  * The Android WebView shell used to package the reference demo. It is maintained
    as a separate project so that its packaging and branding questions do not have to
    gate this toolchain.


